{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790970229,"nonce":"eAPDaXLzBNY3bXwOjO6TZoJtZZs=","title":"A property's own accessor does not bypass itself inside a nested closure","message":"Row: Issue6375.\n\nHaxe writes the backing field directly inside the property's accessor, closures nested in it\nincluded. `is_inside_own_accessor` (ir/mir/field/access.rs) and `static_property_accessor`\n(helpers/globals.rs) look only at `builder.current_function()`, and a lifted lambda is its own\nfunction: `rollback = () -\u003e memberField = 3` calls `set_memberField` again.","files":null}]}